    "The cases preflight runs every component on, in Python (src/pages/components.py) and in the browser's file (src/pages/components.js, in node), comparing the two answers byte for byte: the check 'every component gives the same answer in Python and in the browser'.",
    "A key is a helper's Python name; the browser's is the same name in camelCase (date_words is dateWords). Each case is the arguments, in order, and may state the answer it wants, which holds both languages to it.",
    "An argument {\"$date\": \"2026-02-19\"} is a date: a datetime.date in Python and its ISO string in the browser, which is handed nothing else. {\"$datetime\": ...} is the same for a moment.",
    "The check fails on a helper with no case here and on any part of a helper no case reaches, in either file, so a new branch comes with the case that runs it."
